{"type":"npc","name":"Eternal Symphony","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":350,"temp":0,"max":350,"details":""},"ac":{"value":36,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":"+2 status to all saves vs. auditory or sonic"},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""},"weaknesses":[{"type":"bludgeoning","value":10,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"sonic","value":15,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","melodian"],"details":"Can't speak"},"level":{"value":15},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Some bards and other skilled musicians dare to do it all. They don't need a band holding them back. An eternal symphony is an amalgamation of an entire orchestra's worth of instruments, created by those who wish to go solo without sacrificing the sonic landscape a band or orchestra can supply. As an added bonus, these massive constructs make great bodyguards.</p><p>Sometimes, these constructs outlive their bandmates, while other times, their creators can't handle the upstaging and abandon their creations to wander alone. Regardless of their situation, these constructs focus their efforts on what they do best: entertaining. This tendency can conflict with those who don't want to be followed by a large walking orchestra.</p><h2>Everyone's a Critic</h2><p>Eternal symphonies can't create new works, but they can play their original repertoire flawlessly, sometimes better than their creator. This can drive some composers wild with jealousy, especially when the eternal symphony's performances are in greater demand than those of the original musician. For their part, an eternal symphony typically has an almost religious veneration for the music first taught to them by their creator, while not particularly liking their creator's new works.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 810/1,850/3,400 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, slashing), armor (medium, heavy), perception item, skill items (Athletics, Performance)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, charisma, constitution, energy resistant (sonic, spirit, vitality, void), mind, mind shield, music, sensory (darkvision), throwing, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Aaron Morder","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":7},"dex":{"mod":4},"con":{"mod":8},"int":{"mod":0},"wis":{"mod":0},"cha":{"mod":9}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":23,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"},{"type":"tremorsense","acuity":"imprecise","range":60}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":29,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":25,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":23,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"athletics":{"base":28},"performance":{"base":33}},"traits":{"value":["construct"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"lg"}}},"_id":"ri3dGbG8YJkuzk13","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/eternal-symphony.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Eternal Symphony","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":2,"height":2,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/eternal-symphony.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":